{"title":"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Comment_of_S1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Comment of S1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Comment_on_S2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Comment on S2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution!</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f0212bfbb21683cd1dc123759df4a68075df625.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\{z : z^{18} = 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/87929df2606eb6fa6357c206a25135f6a5183ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\{w : w^{48} = 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" /> are both sets of complex <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roots_of_unity\" title=\"Roots of unity\">roots of unity</a>.  The set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8456bee00fa935518a24fa392387db23559e945e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\{zw : z \\in A ~ \\mbox{and} ~ w \\in B\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" /> is also a set of complex roots of unity.  How many distinct elements are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb5d34a8b2a73764c0a08ebf9f89cc09285ec48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{}^{}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Least_common_multiple\" title=\"Least common multiple\">least common multiple</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, so define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf945b2e3cd1454aa8fdf122d9b41e0dc8391a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = e^{2\\pi i/144}$\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />. We can write the numbers of set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffbe10f26b5e7d1e6ade36991552e5fe1de6bf59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{n^8, n^{16}, \\ldots n^{144}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" /> and of set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc10165db4a03095e4f59f16bb588f278ff96932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{n^3, n^6, \\ldots n^{144}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"19\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b11f15d704bd8adaf3b18dd449868839b57d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^x$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> can yield at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> different values. All solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c238a0e2fe6d3fd49d5219a4b5fabdbf6b5fb4f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$zw$\" width=\"22\" height=\"8\" /> will be in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c90a6f33cf27d347b562c721bd06a557a530f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{8k_1 + 3k_2}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime, and by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chicken_McNugget_Theorem\" title=\"Chicken McNugget Theorem\">Chicken McNugget Theorem</a>, for two relatively prime integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, the largest number that cannot be expressed as the sum of multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fb1087d00e12ae7b46bd97f43b6153ea644471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\cdot b - a - b$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7ad5a23234ccf027e85c677dd1f1428775bf830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />; however, we can easily see that the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d00d6cfbf7dab73af54367e971ffc25a4091499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$145$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e87f45865ddff62782e744d1af671f85659ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$157$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> can be written in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7ad5a23234ccf027e85c677dd1f1428775bf830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />. Since the exponents are of roots of unities, they reduce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/357ce8c6e8b1f6b265150885365871822eeed7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, so all numbers in the range are covered. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a842c2b8241b1784706e13c86f350656b7208be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Comment_of_S1\">Comment of S1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Comment of S1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chicken_McNugget_Theorem\" title=\"Chicken McNugget Theorem\">Chicken McNugget Theorem</a> and the property of complex numbers for reasoning is sharp, but note that the Frobenius Number is only constrained to positive integer pairs. Please check on \"Comment of S2\" below to see how to use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diophantine_equation\" title=\"Diophantine equation\">Diophantine equation</a> to make a simple deduction. ~ Will_Dai\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The 18 and 48th roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be found by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Moivre%27s_Theorem\" title=\"De Moivre&#39;s Theorem\">De Moivre's Theorem</a>. They are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/839d064b201bcc50282f0b2b3504914a99c021e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}\\,\\left(\\frac{2\\pi k_1}{18}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"88\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/6888795676076912fb9237d225cc707c19d9c407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}\\,\\left(\\frac{2\\pi k_2}{48}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"88\" height=\"43\" /> respectively, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195ea2fa9645acd17e758631d7d78e3d333ef086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis}\\,\\theta = \\cos \\theta + i \\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> are integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae2248e6b190df9747a7caa54d785db65a3137c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$zw = \\text{cis}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi k_1}{9} + \\frac{\\pi k_2}{24}\\right) = \\text{cis}\\,\\left(\\frac{8\\pi k_1 + 3 \\pi k_2}{72}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"361\" height=\"45\" />. Since the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometry\" title=\"Trigonometry\">trigonometric</a> functions are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Periodic_function\" title=\"Periodic function\">periodic</a> every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebaedd5298e275f84c171fa1b9acaccab16dcf6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72 \\cdot 2 = \\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" /> distinct elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. As above, all of these will work.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Comment_on_S2\">Comment on S2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Comment on S2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>By the property of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diophantine_equation\" title=\"Diophantine equation\">Diophantine equation</a>, given a problem to find integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9fb4aacd55efaa8c9ee5749b4b75aa7067ee43e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax + by = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> for some integer constants <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />: if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1a646aa72373ac52f63c2273ce82781d9b58a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a, b) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, then any arbitrary integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> could by formed with some combination of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />. Double checking the constraints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, we realize that all integers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad5670c088230d1f258dacea67cb0dcd185ecbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 143]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> can be formed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9a12d5cc2c03aa680df5be62347db149993f4a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8k_1 + 3k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />, yielding the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />.\n~Will_Dai\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The values in polar form will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30bb29f5cfcd79c618215c921191a9c4f11ec888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 20x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f247cfa738ef5869440bdd7aaf51cbe261ed1ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 7.5x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. Multiplying these gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f684e96ba509aa92d751ae4eedb6b2ae7da67a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 27.5x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />. Then, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/4468e25bacc4ccdc53a6775bafbb1cb2bf055215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27.5$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79030abeb688469b5ffc2e1c4e37fee225a529e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/4830a83f9bccd1a0ce12b2e5c74c288301e2fefd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$82.5$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79dc7d13216568e73c831d7b8c14c1a30f7831a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9cacf2e700dd9af8f30a8ff4458824cedbbb6d3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$...$\" width=\"13\" height=\"2\" /> up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d877bfecca8beeb47c32a742db338fe95c9a64e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3960$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/87899ed5e7394bbf6ecb26b4d125e232dc18ebce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\text{lcm}(55,360)) \\implies \\frac{3960 \\cdot 2}{55}=\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"284\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution!\">Video Solution!</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution!\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hdamWTu_F94\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hdamWTu_F94</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME\" title=\"1990 AIME\">1990 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1990 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1990\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1990 AIME Proble